    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3). `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler):\n\n1. **New `normalizeAddress` helper** \u2014 strips and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands common street-type abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) via a token-based lookup (`ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` map). A `null` address normalizes to the empty string.\n\n2. **Store & return the normalized address** \u2014 `addOwner` now calls `owner.setAddress(normalizeAddress(owner.getAddress()))` before persisting, so the stored and returned `address` is normalized (e.g. `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`).\n\n3. **Required-field check rejects blank-after-normalization** \u2014 `validateRequiredOwnerFields` now checks `isBlank(normalizeAddress(...))`, so an address like `\"   \"` (empty after normalization) yields a 400.\n\n4. **All address comparisons use the normalized form** \u2014 `rejectDuplicateHousehold`, `assignHousehold`, and `householdId` now compare via `normalizeAddress` for both the new and existing owners, so household duplicate detection and the shared household id key operate on the normalized address (with abbreviation expansion), not just case/whitespace folding.\n\nLast name comparison still uses the existing `normalizeForComparison`; only the address handling changed, matching the spec.",
